{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"init","kind":"keyword"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"value","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLAccidentalValue","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAccidentalValue","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL18MXLAccidentalValueO"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"smufl","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLSmuflAccidentalGlyphName","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSmuflAccidentalGlyphName","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL27MXLSmuflAccidentalGlyphNameV"},{"text":"? = nil)","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"parameters":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The value of this element.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"value"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The SMuFL canonical glyph name used to specify a particular accidental character.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"smufl"}],"kind":"parameters"}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLKeyAccidental\/init(value:smufl:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Creates a new "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MXLKeyAccidental"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLKeyAccidental"]]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlkeyaccidental\/init(value:smufl:)"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"title":"init(value:smufl:)","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL16MXLKeyAccidentalV5value5smuflAcA18MXLAccidentalValueO_AA08MXLSmuflD9GlyphNameVSgtcfc","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"value","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLAccidentalValue","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL18MXLAccidentalValueO"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"smufl","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLSmuflAccidentalGlyphName","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL27MXLSmuflAccidentalGlyphNameV"},{"text":"?)","kind":"text"}],"symbolKind":"init","role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Initializer"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLKeyAccidental":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The key-accidental type indicates the accidental to be displayed in a non-traditional key signature,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"represented in the same manner as the accidental type without the formatting attributes."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLKeyAccidental"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLKeyAccidental"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLKeyAccidental","title":"MXLKeyAccidental","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlkeyaccidental","type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLKeyAccidental/init(value:smufl:)":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Creates a new "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MXLKeyAccidental"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLKeyAccidental\/init(value:smufl:)","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"init"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"value"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL18MXLAccidentalValueO","text":"MXLAccidentalValue"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"smufl"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL27MXLSmuflAccidentalGlyphNameV","text":"MXLSmuflAccidentalGlyphName"},{"kind":"text","text":"?)"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlkeyaccidental\/init(value:smufl:)","title":"init(value:smufl:)","role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLAccidentalValue":{"title":"MXLAccidentalValue","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLAccidentalValue","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The accidental-value type represents notated accidentals supported by MusicXML. In the MusicXML 2.0 DTD this","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"was a string with values that could be included. The XSD strengthens the data typing to an enumerated list.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The quarter- and three-quarters- accidentals are Tartini-style quarter-tone accidentals. The -down and -up","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"accidentals are quarter-tone accidentals that include arrows pointing down or up. The slash- accidentals are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"used in Turkish classical music. The numbered sharp and flat accidentals are superscripted versions of the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"accidental signs, used in Turkish folk music. The sori and koron accidentals are microtonal sharp and flat","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"accidentals used in Iranian and Persian music. The other accidental covers accidentals other than those listed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"here. It is usually used in combination with the smufl attribute to specify a particular SMuFL accidental. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"smufl attribute may be used with any accidental value to help specify the appearance of symbols that share the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"same MusicXML semantics.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAccidentalValue","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLAccidentalValue","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlaccidentalvalue"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLSmuflAccidentalGlyphName":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlsmuflaccidentalglyphname","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSmuflAccidentalGlyphName","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLSmuflAccidentalGlyphName"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The smufl-accidental-glyph-name type is used to reference a specific Standard Music Font Layout (SMuFL)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"accidental character. The value is a SMuFL canonical glyph name that starts with one of the strings used at"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the start of glyph names for SMuFL accidentals."}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLSmuflAccidentalGlyphName"}],"title":"MXLSmuflAccidentalGlyphName"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","title":"IvorMXL","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","kind":"symbol"}}}